From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: restore requested WDS mode after peer authorization

hostapd may move a station into its four-address AP/VLAN before applying
the association and authorization parameters. The driver caches that WDS
has been enabled, but subsequent firmware peer setup can leave data
frames hitting the unauthenticated-WDS error path.

Reapply a previously requested four-address configuration after peer
authorization. Keep the Direct Switch exclusion in effect across either
ordering of VLAN assignment and authorization.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -7523,6 +7523,18 @@
 			ath12k_warn(ab, "Failed to authorize station: %pM\n",
 				    arsta->addr);
 			goto exit;
+		}
+		/* hostapd can assign the AP/VLAN before the station association
+		 * parameters reach firmware. Reapply WDS after authorization so
+		 * peer association cannot leave the requested mode ineffective.
+		 */
+		if (arsta->ahsta->enable_4addr) {
+			ret = ath12k_mac_sta_set_4addr(hw->wiphy, arsta->ahsta);
+			if (ret) {
+				ath12k_warn(ab, "Failed to restore 4addr station %pM: %d\n",
+					    arsta->addr, ret);
+				goto exit;
+			}
 		}
 		if (ath12k_ab_to_dp(ab)->ops->ds_sta_state) {
 			int ds_ret;
